    "notationLabel": "Trilinear Notation — reproduction study",
    "notationFootnote": "",
    "author": "José A. Sotorrio",
    "description": "Reproduction study — inspired by Trilinear Notation (José A. Sotorrio, 2017; basic version). Minor-third staff at E/G/A# with a C# ledger shown for C and C# (operator effective-ledger rule); three notehead glyphs cycle by diminished-7th set in the operator's x/circle/triangle sequence: X on the below-line set {C,D#,F#,A}, the always-hollow real CIRCLE (O, a ring — not a conventional oval) on the on-line set {C#,E,G,A#}, and left-pointing ◁ triangles on the above-line set {D,F,G#,B}. The X and ◁ glyphs are geometric approximations. Duration is stem-flag-only with a direction-dependent half-note tick (E3, unimplemented) — documented as a deviation. Built from the public gallery description/image; not endorsed by or derived from the original.",
    "systemName": "Trilinear Notation",
    "systemCreator": "José A. Sotorrio",
